\subsubsection{Piece (Block) Message Handler}

The piece message handler is the core data reception path in BitTorrent. When a
peer sends us block data, we need to:

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Validate}: Ensure the block matches a pending request. This prevents
  amplification attacks where a malicious peer sends unrequested data to consume
  memory or overwrite legitimate data with garbage.
\item \textbf{Store}: Copy the block data into the in-progress piece buffer at the
  correct offset.
\item \textbf{Verify}: When all blocks are received, compute the SHA1 hash and compare
  it against the expected hash from the torrent metadata.
\end{enumerate}

The data flow for incoming blocks is:

\begin{verbatim}
peer sends Piece { index, begin, block }
    |
    v
validate against pending_requests
    |
    +-- no match --> return UnexpectedBlock
    |
    v (match found, remove from pending)
store in InProgressPiece via receive_block()
    |
    +-- error --> return UnexpectedBlock
    |
    v
check is_complete()
    |
    +-- false --> return BlockStored
    |
    v (piece complete)
verify_piece(data, expected_hash)
    |
    +-- Ok --> return PieceVerified(index)
    +-- Err --> return PieceHashFailed(index)
\end{verbatim}

The [[PieceHandleResult]] enum captures these outcomes, allowing the caller to
take appropriate action (write to disk, broadcast have, retry download, etc.).

<<incoming message handlers>>=
/// Result of processing a piece (block) message.
///
/// This enum captures the possible outcomes when a peer sends us block data.
/// The variants allow the caller to take appropriate action:
///
/// - `BlockStored`: Normal case, continue downloading
/// - `PieceVerified`: Celebrate, write to disk, broadcast have
/// - `PieceHashFailed`: Log warning, mark piece for retry
/// - `UnexpectedBlock`: Possible protocol violation or duplicate, ignore
///
/// # Example
///
/// ```
/// use literate_bittorrent::client::PieceHandleResult;
///
/// fn process_result(result: PieceHandleResult) {
///     match result {
///         PieceHandleResult::BlockStored => {
///             // Continue downloading, nothing special to do
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::PieceVerified(index) => {
///             println!("Piece {} complete and verified!", index);
///             // Write to disk, broadcast have message
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::PieceHashFailed(index) => {
///             println!("Piece {} failed verification, will retry", index);
///             // Mark piece for re-download
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::UnexpectedBlock => {
///             // Ignore, possibly log at debug level
///         }
///     }
/// }
/// ```
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum PieceHandleResult {
    /// Block received and stored, piece still incomplete.
    BlockStored,
    /// Piece is now complete and verified successfully.
    ///
    /// The contained value is the piece index that was verified.
    PieceVerified(usize),
    /// Piece is complete but hash verification failed.
    ///
    /// The contained value is the piece index that failed verification.
    /// The piece should be marked for retry.
    PieceHashFailed(usize),
    /// Block was unexpected (no matching pending request).
    ///
    /// This can happen due to:
    /// - Duplicate blocks after a request timeout and retry
    /// - Malicious peers sending unrequested data
    /// - Race conditions during choke/unchoke
    UnexpectedBlock,
}

/// Handles an incoming piece (block) message.
///
/// This is the core data reception path. The function:
/// 1. Validates the block matches a pending request
/// 2. Stores the block in the in-progress piece
/// 3. If piece is complete, verifies the SHA1 hash
///
/// # Security: Request Validation
///
/// We validate that incoming blocks match pending requests to prevent
/// amplification attacks and data corruption. Without this check, a
/// malicious peer could:
/// - Send unrequested blocks to consume memory
/// - Overwrite legitimate data with garbage
/// - Cause hash verification failures
///
/// # Data Integrity: Hash Verification
///
/// When a piece is complete, we immediately verify its SHA1 hash against
/// the expected hash from the torrent metadata. This is critical because:
/// - Peers may be malicious or buggy
/// - Network corruption can occur
/// - The torrent file's hashes are the only source of truth
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `conn` - The peer connection that sent the block
/// * `index` - Piece index (0-based)
/// * `begin` - Byte offset within the piece
/// * `block` - The block data
/// * `in_progress` - The in-progress piece being assembled
/// * `expected_hash` - The expected SHA1 hash for verification
///
/// # Returns
///
/// `PieceHandleResult` indicating what happened:
/// - `BlockStored`: block saved, piece incomplete
/// - `PieceVerified`: piece complete and hash matches
/// - `PieceHashFailed`: piece complete but hash mismatch
/// - `UnexpectedBlock`: no matching pending request or receive failed
///
/// # Example
///
/// ```no_run
/// use literate_bittorrent::client::{PeerConnection, PieceHandleResult, handle_incoming_piece};
/// use literate_bittorrent::pieces::InProgressPiece;
///
/// fn process_piece_message(
///     conn: &mut PeerConnection,
///     index: u32,
///     begin: u32,
///     block: &[u8],
///     in_progress: &mut InProgressPiece,
///     expected_hash: &[u8; 20],
/// ) {
///     match handle_incoming_piece(conn, index, begin, block, in_progress, expected_hash) {
///         PieceHandleResult::BlockStored => {
///             // Request more blocks if needed
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::PieceVerified(idx) => {
///             // Write piece to disk
///             // Broadcast have message to all peers
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::PieceHashFailed(idx) => {
///             // Reset the in-progress piece
///             // Re-request all blocks
///         }
///         PieceHandleResult::UnexpectedBlock => {
///             // Ignore or track for rate limiting
///         }
///     }
/// }
/// ```
pub fn handle_incoming_piece(
    conn: &mut PeerConnection,
    index: u32,
    begin: u32,
    block: &[u8],
    in_progress: &mut InProgressPiece,
    expected_hash: &[u8; 20],
) -> PieceHandleResult {
    // Find and remove matching pending request
    let request_pos = conn.state.pending_requests.iter().position(|req| {
        req.piece_index == index && req.offset == begin && req.length == block.len() as u32
    });

    match request_pos {
        None => {
            debug!(
                piece = index,
                offset = begin,
                len = block.len(),
                "received unexpected block - no matching request"
            );
            return PieceHandleResult::UnexpectedBlock;
        }
        Some(pos) => {
            conn.state.pending_requests.remove(pos);
        }
    }

    // Store the block
    match in_progress.receive_block(begin, block) {
        Err(e) => {
            warn!(
                piece = index,
                offset = begin,
                error = %e,
                "block receive failed"
            );
            return PieceHandleResult::UnexpectedBlock;
        }
        Ok(false) => {
            // Duplicate block, already received
            debug!(
                piece = index,
                offset = begin,
                "duplicate block received"
            );
            return PieceHandleResult::BlockStored;
        }
        Ok(true) => {
            // Block stored successfully
        }
    }

    // Check if piece is complete
    if !in_progress.is_complete() {
        return PieceHandleResult::BlockStored;
    }

    // Verify hash
    let data = in_progress.data();
    match verify_piece(index, data, expected_hash) {
        Ok(()) => {
            info!(
                piece = index,
                bytes = data.len(),
                "piece verified successfully"
            );
            PieceHandleResult::PieceVerified(index as usize)
        }
        Err(e) => {
            warn!(
                piece = index,
                error = %e,
                "piece hash verification failed"
            );
            PieceHandleResult::PieceHashFailed(index as usize)
        }
    }
}
